      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>those are good starting points for the roles, but they're a bit abstract. i want to make them feel more grounded and \"real\" for the setting. can you give these characters more specific backgrounds? like, what's their ethnicity or cultural vibe? i want to make sure the \"street\" characters feel like they actually belong in those rough, gritty parts of the city to create that authentic contrast with the detective.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
