      "content": "To ground your characters, consider the **Apocalyptic Kirk** as a first-generation immigrant from a Balkan slum who uses hyper-technical weaponry he built while working as a day laborer, blending crude Brooklyn grit with calculated efficiency. The **Narcotic Lady** could be a Black woman raised in the projects who speaks a distinct sub-culture slang, acting as a terrifyingly gentle matriarch who controls her territory through a network of street families rather than a formal organization. Finally, the **Power Broker** might be a wealthy, avuncular tragedy figure—an old-guard Italian mob boss with a crumbling empire who views the detective's intellect as a personal insult, forcing him into a dangerous duel of moral logic versus literal force. These specific cultural textures will make the danger feel immediate and visceral to your audience.",
